<title>UK: Freepages to raise 40 million stg.</title>
<headline>Freepages to raise 40 million stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Information services company, the Freepages Group, said on Tuesday that it would raise 40 million stg via a U.S. public offering and related Nasdaq listing with an international offering.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co International would act as global co-ordinator to the issues.  </p>
<p>Freepages said the net proceeds would be used to fund joint ventures including one with Verenigde Nederlandse Uitgeversbedrijven B.V. for expansion into the Netherlands.</p>
<p>The company also intends to expand into Belgium and Luxembourg.</p>
<p>The firm reported sales of 2.5 million stg for the quarter ended December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
